    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72-a5">

                <pb facs="0191" n="103" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg103"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 5.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Doctor Rio Branco to Mr. Thompson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-09-30"><hi rendition="#italic">September 30,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of your excellency’s note of the 9th
                    instant, asking for my attention to your note of May 25 last, on the use by a
                    line of Brazilian merchant vessels plying between Bahia and Pelotas of a flag
                    much resembling the national ensign of the United States.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to say to your excellency that I have brought your note to the
                    knowledge of my colleague of the navy department, whose reply I am awaiting in
                    order to, in due time, transmit it to you, to whom I have the pleasure of
                    reiterating the protests of my high consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio Branco.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
